*** Add File:README_LEVEL4_FINAL.md
+# Aegis Level‑4 Finalization
+
+This patch finalizes the Level‑4 production readiness items:
+
+- Helm overlays with production resource sizing for webhook & calibrator
+- Kustomize production settings (failurePolicy=Fail)
+- M‑of‑N service with OIDC-based approver authentication
+- CrypTen worker entrypoint + k8s StatefulSet for distributed MPC pilots
+- Production Prometheus alert rules and Grafana dashboard for SLOs
+- Compliance packet templates and auditor intake helpers + workflows
+
+How to proceed (high level)
+1) Populate secrets (KUBE_CONFIG_DATA, EVIDENCE_BUCKET, COSIGN_KMS_URI, AWS_*, OIDC_JWKS_URL, OIDC_AUDIENCE, GF_API_KEY, MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI)
+2) Build & push images (webhook, calibrator, canary-signing, crypten-worker)
+3) Deploy in staging: install Prometheus/Flagger/Istio, apply canary & signing services, and run the one-click staging drill
+4) Run MPC pilot using crypten-worker StatefulSet and generate test vectors for the auditor
+5) Assemble compliance packet and share with auditors
+
+Notes:
+- The OIDC enhancement requires a jwks URL and audience; without these the M‑of‑N service will accept approvals supplied in the request body (less secure).
+- The distributed CrypTen setup is for staging/pilot and uses headless service + StatefulSet; use real CA and mTLS certs in production.
+- The Prometheus rules and dashboard are tuned examples; adjust thresholds according to your traffic profile.
+
